{"nodes": [{"id": "readme_optimizador_pc", "label": "Optimizador PC README", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L1-L19", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Windows 11 Pro optimizer: WPF UI written entirely in PowerShell 5.1, packaged as a single-file portable .exe with ps2exe. State: complete UI plus bounded real changes, expanding."}, {"id": "readme_ps2exe", "label": "ps2exe (PowerShell-to-exe compiler)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L3", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Accepts a single input file, which is why build.ps1 exists; installed in CurrentUser if missing."}, {"id": "readme_single_responsibility", "label": "One responsibility per file (a change opens one file)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L25-L26", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_category_index", "label": "CategoryIndex: order, visibility and lock of sections", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L203-L240", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Main file of the sections; content stays in ui/Data/Categories. Visible = $false hides without deleting; Locked = $true shows a padlock, a notice, disabled controls and Reset off (IsEnabled = $false). A file not in the index still appears at the end, unlocked (Get-UnlistedCategories), so adding a section is just creating a file."}, {"id": "readme_navigation_index", "label": "NavigationIndex: sidebar buttons as data", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L242-L283", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Does for sidebar buttons what CategoryIndex does for sections; fields Group (Top/Bottom), Visible, Locked, View ($null = no navigation), Default, Icon. Adding a menu entry is adding a line; FindName('NavSettings') still works."}, {"id": "readme_languages", "label": "Adding a language (Register-Language, LanguageIndex)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L296-L339", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each Lang file is an 'English text' -> 'translation' dictionary; copy es.ps1 and add a line to LanguageIndex.ps1. Get-MissingTranslations 'es' returns exactly what is missing because T records every request. Language names are never translated (TranslateOptions = $false in 10-Language.ps1)."}, {"id": "readme_preferences", "label": "Preferences: Settings screen built from ui/Data/Preferences", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L341-L382", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Adding an option is creating a Register-Preference file; the view is untouched. Type Toggle or Choice (Options fixed or a scriptblock); Get/Set use Get-AppSetting / Set-AppSetting."}, {"id": "readme_register_category", "label": "Declaring a section (Register-Category, New-Setting)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L384-L416", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "New-Setting infers the control: with -Options a dropdown, without it a toggle. Only Id, Name, Icon, Description and Items are required."}, {"id": "readme_defined_categories", "label": "Defined categories (Regedit, Internet, Cleanup, Power, Update)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L614-L628", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Regedit 47 settings, Internet 27 steps, Cleanup 15 steps, Power 2 steps, Update 2 settings. Badges count settings with -Badge 'NEW' unless declared by hand; list pill counters are still fixed values while the detail row counts real status."}, {"id": "readme_module_diagram", "label": "Module diagram (load order and who uses whom)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L452-L495", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Numbered arrows are load order, the rest usage; no arrow leaves core/ towards Components or Views because core/ does not know the interface."}, {"id": "readme_design_system", "label": "Design system and live theme switch", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L497-L536", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "All appearance comes from MainWindow.xaml resources: palette, gradients, Window.Resources brushes, styles, UiKit components, Segoe UI Variable, Segoe Fluent Icons. XAML uses DynamicResource and code SetResourceReference, so Set-AppTheme only rewrites brush colors and the built UI repaints without rebuilding views."}, {"id": "readme_view_containers", "label": "Shell containers (HeaderTitleArea, HeaderActionsArea, MainContent) via PageHeader", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L538-L548", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Views are built in code and injected into three named containers through PageHeader.ps1, so changing screens never recreates the window and all screens share the header."}, {"id": "readme_effects_transitions", "label": "Effects and transitions table", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L550-L575", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Staggered entry, view entry (fade + 14px slide, 260 ms CubicEase), card lift (3px + section-color halo, 170 ms), backdrop (3 radial blobs, 27-41 s, 20 fps), nav indicator (QuinticEase), toggle (ColorAnimation + BackEase), count-up, press-shrink via XAML triggers, 6-8px scrollbar."}, {"id": "readme_navigation_flow", "label": "Navigation flow (OptimizationsList <-> CategoryDetail, Settings)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L595-L612", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_build_pipeline", "label": "build.ps1 combine + compile pipeline", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L633-L676", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "ps2exe accepts one input file and the .exe must be portable, so build.ps1 reads main.ps1 line by line, pastes embedded folders and the XAML into build/_combined.ps1 (generated, never edit) and calls Invoke-ps2exe -noConsole -requireAdmin to produce build/OptimizadorPC.exe. -CombineOnly skips ps2exe."}, {"id": "readme_test_coverage", "label": "Test coverage (core, UI, main.ps1 wiring, rules, security invariants)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L680-L697", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "core/ against the real registry (read states, signed DWord, writes against an HKCU branch); UI with real WPF controls without a window; main.ps1 wiring by pressing buttons (only way to catch convention 4); source rules (BOM, closures, glyphs, nothing left out of the .exe); security invariants (allowlisted -Registry paths, no dynamic code or network in ui/core, ExternalLink only http/https). Playwright does not apply (WPF, no DOM)."}, {"id": "readme_pending_work", "label": "Pending work (rollback, restore point, Update -Registry, ...)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L747-L767", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Persistent rollback and undo; restore-point warning before the first elevated write; -Registry for Actualizaciones; services/tasks/policies as new core/ subfolders; real values for settings without -Registry; Quick Actions and Reset; computed list counters; .exe smoke test with UI Automation; search over steps and guides; remember ticked steps; a back-to-DHCP step."}, {"id": "readme_skipif_idempotent_steps", "label": "-SkipIf skips already-done steps (Energia power plan at fixed GUID)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L737-L739", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The original .bat created a new copy of the Ultimate Performance plan on every run; the step uses a fixed GUID and -SkipIf (a registry value) to skip it if already present."}], "edges": [{"source": "claude_layer_engine", "target": "ui_engine_categoryregistry", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L65", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_layer_engine", "target": "ui_engine_preferenceregistry", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L66", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_layer_engine", "target": "ui_engine_guideregistry", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L67", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_layer_engine", "target": "ui_engine_markdown", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L68", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_layer_engine", "target": "ui_engine_search", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L69", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_layer_engine", "target": "ui_engine_translation", "relation": "references", "conf